  "preamble": "In Southern Bantu, the Proto-Bantu palatal consonant *c (and voiced *j) developed into the voiceless alveolar lateral fricative [ɬ], written hl. Van der Vlugt and Gunnink (2025) show that alveolar lateral obstruents reconstruct to Proto-Nguni as the regular reflex of Proto-Bantu *c and *j; the same outcome appears in Sotho, while Tswana has the lateral affricate tlh [tɬʰ]. The exact phonetic value of Proto-Bantu *c (palatal stop or affricate) is reconstructed, and its precise phonetic starting point is debated.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Lateralization, Spirantization, Fronting",
